        "instruction": {
          "title": "Summary and Recap",
          "description": "To recap: we observed Mars's apparent westward loop in the night sky. We saw how the geocentric model required complicated epicycles, while the heliocentric model neatly explained it through Earth overtaking slower outer planets. We connected the orbital geometry to the line-of-sight perspective, and saw how distance reduces the retrograde effect for Jupiter and Saturn. You have successfully completed the lab!"
